INSERT INTO `quest_description_conditional` (`QuestId`, `PlayerConditionId`, `QuestgiverCreatureId`, `locale`, `Text`, `OrderIndex`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(92617, 144999, 0, 'enUS', 'First Tuktuk runs, then Brakko runs. Cannot be the only one still fighting.\n\nZiny will fail by Ziny\'s self. Fight is too hard alone, will not be strong enough.\n\nDo not want to fail. Cannot let the Fungal Fellowship down!\n\nHad choice, fail or run.\n\nBut run was also fail. Ziny very sorry to $p!\n\nCan practice, fight big and scary enemies together?', 3, 66102), -- Mushrooming Resilience
(92617, 144998, 0, 'enUS', 'First Tuktuk runs, then Brakko runs. Cannot be the only one still fighting.\n\nZiny will fail by Ziny\'s self. Fight is too hard alone, will not be strong enough.\n\nDo not want to fail. Cannot let the Puffguard down!\n\nHad choice, fail or run.\n\nBut run was also fail. Ziny very sorry to $p!\n\nCan practice, fight big and scary enemies together?', 2, 66102), -- Mushrooming Resilience
(92617, 144997, 0, 'enUS', 'First Tuktuk runs, then Brakko runs. Cannot be the only one still fighting.\n\nZiny will fail by Ziny\'s self. Fight is too hard alone, will not be strong enough.\n\nDo not want to fail. Cannot let the Sporesworn down!\n\nHad choice, fail or run.\n\nBut run was also fail. Ziny very sorry to $p!\n\nCan practice, fight big and scary enemies together?', 1, 66102), -- Mushrooming Resilience
(92617, 144996, 0, 'enUS', 'First Tuktuk runs, then Brakko runs. Cannot be the only one still fighting.\n\nZiny will fail by Ziny\'s self. Fight is too hard alone, will not be strong enough.\n\nDo not want to fail. Cannot let the Ringcaps down!\n\nHad choice, fail or run.\n\nBut run was also fail. Ziny very sorry to $p!\n\nCan practice, fight big and scary enemies together?', 0, 66102), -- Mushrooming Resilience
(92616, 144999, 0, 'enUS', 'Brakko sorry that Brakko let $p and Fungal Fellosh down.\n\nBrakko is much scared of sporegliders. Could sneak up at Brakko above cap, where cannot see. Could really hurt cap!\n\nVery sorry, $p. Brakko doesn\'t think Brakko can be tank for team.\n\nUnless... $p practice sporegliders with Brakko?', 3, 66102), -- Mushrooming Courage
(92616, 144998, 0, 'enUS', 'Brakko sorry that Brakko let $p and Puffguard down.\n\nBrakko is much scared of sporegliders. Could sneak up at Brakko above cap, where cannot see. Could really hurt cap!\n\nVery sorry, $p. Brakko doesn\'t think Brakko can be tank for team.\n\nUnless... $p practice sporegliders with Brakko?', 2, 66102), -- Mushrooming Courage
(92616, 144997, 0, 'enUS', 'Brakko sorry that Brakko let $p and Sporesworn down.\n\nBrakko is much scared of sporegliders. Could sneak up at Brakko above cap, where cannot see. Could really hurt cap!\n\nVery sorry, $p. Brakko doesn\'t think Brakko can be tank for team.\n\nUnless... $p practice sporegliders with Brakko?', 1, 66102), -- Mushrooming Courage
(92616, 144996, 0, 'enUS', 'Brakko sorry that Brakko let $p and Ringcaps down.\n\nBrakko is much scared of sporegliders. Could sneak up at Brakko above cap, where cannot see. Could really hurt cap!\n\nVery sorry, $p. Brakko doesn\'t think Brakko can be tank for team.\n\nUnless... $p practice sporegliders with Brakko?', 0, 66102), -- Mushrooming Courage
(92603, 148574, 254012, 'enUS', 'The shade is my doing... my mistake. The Void here is so pure, so... alive, and I was foolish. I\'d seen shades before: ren\'dorei shadows made manifest. I thought I could make my own.\n\nBut it\'s wrong. Broken. I can\'t escape it anymore than I can escape my own thoughts.\n\nThat\'s why I\'m here. I sought the Void for a solution and a voice led me north. It promises an artifact that will rid me of this failure.', 0, 66102), -- O Lonely Star
(92496, 146074, 251669, 'enUS', 'Idago\'s safe thanks to you, but de Twilight\'s Blade threat remains!\n\nDe cultists say they\'re takin\' orders from Deathchanter Mish\'mosh. Dis cultist must be behind the death and destruction brought to our sedge.\n\nFor the honor of the people we lost, root this snake out of our home!', 0, 66102), -- Spears Against de Shadow
(92325, 23503, 250410, 'enUS', 'My sister Krenna was once a Conqueror in the Horde\'s armies. Ruthless. Brutal. Some said a tyrant. But she was different when we were young. Warm to those she would let in. Scared, but always kind to me. Did power change her? \n\nAnd if it changed her, did it change Garrosh Hellscream? I know who Krenna was. I do not know who Garrosh was.\n\nTravel to Nagrand and find out. Do not worry about encroaching on Horde territory. The magic of the portal will disguise you.', 0, 66102), -- Hellscream's Heritage
(91606, 20069, 256901, 'enUS', 'A waste. This creature would be glorious on the battlefield, with its mind intact.\n\nThere is no undoing shadowgrafting. Only killing.\n\nSo, we kill it. But it is strong. Vidious and I will need time to weaken it.\n\nMeanwhile, find this domanaar\'s grafter. It is the one responsible for this travesty. End it.\n\nThat will draw out our enemy. Then, it\'s their turn.', 0, 66102), -- Voidscar Arena: Clearing House
(91605, 20069, 256815, 'enUS', 'So, you are one of these Horde renegades Ziadan has recruited? I see the appeal.\n\nThe Voidscar Arena is crawling with Void monsters once again. A domanaar rules here, I have no doubt.\n\nThey have not yet emerged to parlay. Our mysterious interloper must not be present. Good.\n\nPut an end to this charade. Destroy their forces. Destroy their resources. And turn their tools against them. Make them feel the disdain I feel for them.\n\nZiadan and I shall investigate this interloper.', 0, 66102), -- Voidscar Arena: The Wrong Side
(91603, 20069, 256813, 'enUS', 'We press on.\n\nShadowgraft requires a potent font to power it--likely more than one, given this many creatures. They will be nearby. Destroy the power sources, then meet us on the next ridge.\n\nRemember: if this domanaar succeeds, their conquest will not end in Slayer\'s Rise. They will find a way to your homeworld. They would shadowgraft Azeroth herself. Put an end to this.\n\nMeanwhile, I suppose I shall relish in this opportunity to observe Ziadan\'s weaknesses up close.', 0, 66102), -- Voidscar Arena: Two Against One
(91545, 47452, 0, 'enUS', 'That must be the monster that killed Hieron. It\'s tearing open a backdoor for the Void\'s forces to pour into Silvermoon.\n\nYou\'re not like the people I left behind in Silvermoon, $n. I\'m doing this for Hieron. But if you want to save your city, I\'ll do it for you too.\n\nSignal Umbric. Let\'s do this. Together.', 0, 66102), -- Stronger Than Before
(91536, 47452, 0, 'enUS', '<Astre looks from Hieron\'s journal to the worn letter. Their expression flickers with anger.>\n\nI ask you, is it right that we ren\'dorei were exiled from Silvermoon? By what right do you sin\'dorei deny us access to our families? To our homes?\n\nBlood elves say we are a threat the Sunwell. This is a lie. The truth is, they are simply afraid of us. Of what they do not understand. Are you?\n\nWe\'re here to protect something of value. Kill any beasts that threaten those flowers for Hieron\'s tea. Silvermoon can save itself.', 0, 66102), -- Like a Weed
(91360, 137020, 246607, 'enUS', 'The roots of the World Trees are infused with both nutrients and the magic of Harandar. As the large vessels that they are, they will draw to them unwanted fauna and flora. Some of them are harmless, but we want to keep the roots clear.\n\nA lot of us are allergic to the green weeds that flourish beside the roots of the World Trees. I hope you aren\'t, or you\'ll find this task difficult!', 0, 66102), -- Weeding Out the Unwanted
(91145, 147872, 245878, 'enUS', 'A domanaar was harrying our back lines. It was... different than the other void beasts--like it was playing rather than fighting. Callum, my partner, led a squad to hunt it down. They never came back.\n\nCallum\'s an Arathi through and through. He wouldn\'t fall here--I know it.\n\nI was already looking for him when the Vanguard was lost at the Voidspire. This place has claimed my friends and comrades, and I\'m not losing Cal too. I know the route his squad took, but I can\'t search alone.', 0, 66102), -- The Conquered Heroes
(90922, 145132, 244980, 'enUS', '<The shade flickers. You can barely make out its whisper.>\n\nYou monster... You... soulless killer...\n\n<Its arm reaches toward you, then dissipates. Somehow, the presence is a familiar one. You feel that you know this spirit. \n\nYou see more flickers in the distance. What are these shades?>', 1, 66102), -- The Fallen Wake
(90922, 145119, 244980, 'enUS', '<The shade flickers. You can barely make out its whisper.>\n\nYou were... never strong enough...\n\n<Its arm reaches toward you, then dissipates. Somehow, the presence is a familiar one. You feel that you know this spirit. \n\nYou see more flickers in the distance. What are these shades?>', 0, 66102), -- The Fallen Wake
(90875, 139629, 241620, 'enUS', 'One more thing before we can return to our refuge. There is a domanaar, whose name is Snaerius. He scrys the vastness of the Great Dark Beyond in search of more victims, more fighters for these pits.\n\nKill him and seize the focus he uses to spy on distant realms. It\'s the last piece of the puzzle.\n\nI wish I could join you in the fight, but I need to get the injured to safety. We will await your return, friend.', 1, 66102), -- Across Worlds
(90875, 67878, 241620, 'enUS', 'One more thing before we can return to our refuge. There is a domanaar, whose name is Snaerius. He scrys the vastness of the Great Dark Beyond in search of more victims--more fighters for these pits.\n\nKill him and seize the focus he uses to spy on distant realms. It\'s the last piece of the puzzle.\n\nI wish I could join you in the fight, but I need to get the injured to safety. We will await your return, $G brother:sister;.', 0, 66102), -- Across Worlds
(90874, 139629, 241620, 'enUS', '<Tul\'amar reaches into a pouch on her hip and retrieves a cracked stone of domanaar make.>\n\nThe voidwalkers carry these. I\'ve been able to use them as spell reagents, and they were helpful for my initial construction of the portal nexus. I presume that they\'ll help me attune it to our world.\n\nBesides that, they deserve death at your hands. Our suffering is their delight. Repay them the favor.', 1, 66102), -- Their Violent Ends
(90874, 67878, 241620, 'enUS', '<Tul\'amar reaches into a pouch on her hip and retrieves a cracked stone of domanaar make.>\n\nThe voidwalkers carry these. I\'ve been able to use them as spell reagents, and they were helpful for my initial construction of the portal nexus. I presume that they\'ll help me attune it to our world.\n\nBesides that, they deserve death at your hands. Our suffering is their delight. Repay them the favor.', 0, 66102), -- Their Violent Ends
(90873, 139629, 241620, 'enUS', 'The domanaar capture us and others across worlds and force us to fight for their amusement. Their fascination with mortals is equal only to their sadism. \n\nI was able to improvise a device from a combination of my magic and the pure chaos of this world and used it to escape. It breaks shackles, both those literal and metaphysical. Using it just once takes a lot out of me.\n\n<Tul\'amar produces the relic and then spends as much of her arcane energy into the device as she can to charge it. She gulps for air with ragged breaths from the effort.>\n\nFree my people and disrupt the gates they used to steal us to this world.\n\nI won\'t let anyone else be left behind. Never again.', 1, 66102), -- These Violent Delights
(90873, 67878, 241620, 'enUS', 'The domanaar capture us and others across worlds and force us to fight for their amusement. Their fascination with mortals is equal only to their sadism. \n\nI was able to improvise a device from a combination of my magic and the pure chaos of this world and used it to escape. It breaks shackles, both those literal and metaphysical. Using it just once takes a lot out of me.\n\n<Tul\'amar produces the relic and then spends as much of her arcane energy into the device as she can to charge it. She gulps for air with ragged breaths from the effort.>\n\nFree our kin and disrupt the gates they used to steal us to this world.\n\nI won\'t let anyone else be left behind. Never again.', 0, 66102), -- These Violent Delights
(90872, 139629, 0, 'enUS', '<Tul\'amar looks away from the blood-soaked and mortified Juras, and toward the portal as it flickers to life. She reads it with her powers of the arcane.>\n\nHe\'ll get over it. Besides, my other theory required Juras and I getting into a fist-fight.\n\nNow, you do the same to the others. The violent energies will power the portal, but attuning it will be a separate matter. When you\'re done here, meet me on the domanaar rise above. With you here, we can finally take what we need.', 1, 66102), -- Drenched In It
(90872, 67878, 241620, 'enUS', '<Tul\'amar looks away from the blood-soaked and mortified Juras, and toward the portal as it flickers to life. She reads it with her powers of the arcane.>\n\nHe\'ll get over it. Besides, my other theory required Juras and I getting into a fist-fight.\n\nNow, you do the same to the others. The violent energies will power the portal, but attuning it will be a separate matter. When you\'re done here, meet me on the domanaar rise above. With you here, we can finally take what we need.', 0, 66102), -- Drenched In It
(90866, 139629, 241620, 'enUS', 'I must return my people to our world. To safety. Below, we\'ve cobbled together a portal nexus with what we\'ve scavenged from the domanaar, but we have not been able to get it to work.\n\nHowever, I witnessed a magical reaction when an argument between two krokul came to blows. It flickered to life, briefly. Like everything else of the Void, I believe domanaar magic resonates with violence.\n\nBring me blood from the beasts of the trench to the north. I have an idea.\n\n<She shows her fangs in a playful snarl before pantomiming a claw swipe.>\n\nBeasts. They have those where you come from, right?', 1, 66102), -- Universal Language
(90866, 67878, 241620, 'enUS', 'I must return my people to our world. To safety. Below, we\'ve cobbled together a portal nexus with what we\'ve scavenged from the domanaar, but we have not been able to get it to work.\n\nHowever, I witnessed a magical reaction when an argument between two krokul came to blows. It flickered to life, briefly. Like everything else of the Void, I believe domanaar magic resonates with violence.\n\nBring me blood from the beasts of the trench to the north. I have an idea.\n\n<She shows her fangs in a playful snarl before pantomiming a claw swipe.>\n\nBeasts. You remember those from Argus, don\'t you? Or are you too young?', 0, 66102), -- Universal Language
(90837, 41722, 0, 'enUS', 'I have been sensing powerful fel magic throughout Silvermoon, but this is the first origin point I could locate. The rest were too faint, or perhaps deliberately hidden. Fortunately, this means we now have a specific area to comb through more closely.\n\nWe need to gather more evidence. Go around this area and see if you can find more hidden sources of fel. I trust your sight should make this a simple task, $ct.', 2, 66102), -- Murder Row: Traces of Fel
(90837, 139931, 0, 'enUS', 'I have been sensing powerful fel magic throughout Silvermoon, but this is the first origin point I could locate. The rest were too faint, or perhaps deliberately hidden. Fortunately, this means we now have a specific area to comb through more closely.\n\nWe need to gather more evidence. Go around this area and see if you can find more hidden sources of fel. I have no fondness for what you are, demon--but if you will use your senses for good, then I have no quarrel with you.', 1, 66102), -- Murder Row: Traces of Fel
(90837, 39987, 0, 'enUS', 'I have been sensing powerful fel magic throughout Silvermoon, but this is the first origin point I could locate. The rest were too faint, or perhaps deliberately hidden. Fortunately, this means we now have a specific area to comb through more closely.\n\nWe need to gather more evidence. Go around this area and see if you can find more hidden sources of fel. I trust your... proclivities will make this an easy task, $c.', 0, 66102), -- Murder Row: Traces of Fel
(90835, 95784, 0, 'enUS', 'Hail, $ct $n. Your arrival is timely, as always.\n\nThe Illidari are performing an investigation in Silvermoon. The details need not be spoken of openly, but Belath Dawnblade specifically requested your aid in the matter.\n\nThe last I heard, he was surveying the upper terraces of the Bazaar.\n\nSeek him out, when you have time.', 0, 66102), -- Murder Row: Rumors Abound
(90782, 122541, 242233, 'enUS', '<The man calls out to you in your native tongue. His accent is unfamiliar to you.>\n\nA $G brother:sister; of Argus! Kin of mine! Lost to us for ages, surely you hail from the... no, my questions can wait. There are more pressing matters.\n\nThese domanaar kidnapped us from our world. Portals opened, and they poured forth from the sky. They force us to fight and die in their arenas for their amusement! I escaped, only to be captured again trying to help my people.\n\nMy elder sister, Tul\'amar, has a plan to get us home. Set me free, and I\'ll take you to her.', 0, 66102), -- The Nethersent
(90622, 144999, 243226, 'enUS', '$p, the Fungal Fellowship look stronger now! More ready. Hope they won\'t run again.\n\nNext fight is against Glow Guard. Glow Guard always never lose.\n\nHope your training makes fight better, before Fungal Fellowship lose.\n\nWill be fun for watch!', 3, 66102), -- Not-Yet Defeated Champions
(90622, 144998, 243226, 'enUS', '$p, the Puffguard look stronger now! More ready. Hope they won\'t run again.\n\nNext fight is against Glow Guard. Glow Guard always never lose.\n\nHope your training makes fight better, before Puffguard lose.\n\nWill be fun for watch!', 2, 66102), -- Not-Yet Defeated Champions
(90622, 144997, 243226, 'enUS', '$p, the Sporesworn look stronger now! More ready. Hope they won\'t run again.\n\nNext fight is against Glow Guard. Glow Guard always never lose.\n\nHope your training makes fight better, before Sporesworn lose.\n\nWill be fun for watch!', 1, 66102), -- Not-Yet Defeated Champions
(90622, 144996, 243226, 'enUS', '$p, the Ringcaps look stronger now! More ready. Hope they won\'t run again.\n\nNext fight is against Glow Guard. Glow Guard always never lose.\n\nHope your training makes fight better, before Ringcaps lose.\n\nWill be fun for watch!', 0, 66102), -- Not-Yet Defeated Champions
(90620, 144999, 243226, 'enUS', 'Fungus... Fellows? Weird name. Who chose?\n\nDon\'t worry about. Ok, ready?\n\nYou and the Fungus Fellows head on down, and we say words.\n\nYou fight Spore Storm. If beat, fight Cap Clash.\n\nIf beat, fight Fungus Force.\n\nAlways-winners are Glow Guard. You won\'t beat.\n\nNo run out! Run out is big, big lose.', 3, 66102), -- To the Ring
(90620, 144998, 243226, 'enUS', 'Puffguard? Not bad. I like!\n\nOk, ready?\n\nYou and the Puffguard head on down, and we say words.\n\nYou fight Spore Storm. If beat, fight Cap Clash.\n\nIf beat, fight Fungus Force.\n\nAlways-winners are Glow Guard. You won\'t beat.\n\nNo run out! Run out is big, big lose.', 2, 66102), -- To the Ring
(90620, 144997, 243226, 'enUS', 'Sporesworn? Not bad. I like!\n\nOk, ready?\n\nYou and the Sporesworn head on down, and we say words.\n\nYou fight Spore Storm. If beat, fight Cap Clash.\n\nIf beat, fight Fungus Force.\n\nAlways-winners are Glow Guard. You won\'t beat.\n\nNo run out! Run out is big, big lose.', 1, 66102), -- To the Ring
(90620, 144996, 243226, 'enUS', 'Ringcaps? Not bad. I like!\n\nOk, ready?\n\nYou and the Ringcaps head on down, and we say words.\n\nYou fight Spore Storm. If beat, fight Cap Clash.\n\nIf beat, fight Fungus Force.\n\nAlways-winners are Glow Guard. You won\'t beat.\n\nNo run out! Run out is big, big lose.', 0, 66102), -- To the Ring
(90484, 93757, 242393, 'enUS', '<Trishe gasps.>\n\nYou\'re my size! You must also be above eleventy five years old! That means you\'re response-able, too!\n\n<Trishe pouts.>\n\nMy friend Steggy is missing! She was here with me, but then there were all these pretty colors and she ran off after them and I was too slow to follow her.\n\nI\'m s\'posed to watch Steggy. I\'m response-able! And now you\'re response-able for finding her, okay?', 0, 66102), -- Sightseeing Stegadon
(89205, 39987, 0, 'enUS', 'I told Zanien here the whole story. He\'s been training warlocks for a long time--and if anyone hates sloppy ones, it\'s him. You can probably relate.\n\nHe\'s confident he can get the wardbreaker recharged. Follow his instructions and we should be good to head out afterward.', 0, 66102), -- Cutting a Key
(86846, 136316, 238072, 'enUS', '$p, Eitrigg told me how you helped save Hammerfall and stop the Red Dawn.\n\nI am working to help them recover and rebuild from the attack with my fellow Sunwalkers: Malu and Nadura.\n\nOne thing they have been doing is gathering supplies needed by Hammerfall\'s crafters from various sources.\n\nIf you could deliver these supplies, it would be a great help.', 0, 66102), -- Resupplying Our Suppliers
(86841, 135389, 237594, 'enUS', 'Alonsus tells me you\'re looking for relics of holy power, Highlord, to sustain those performing the ritual holding the Void at bay.\n\nTake what you need in service to the Light, and let me know if there\'s anything else you require.', 0, 66102), -- Relics of Paladins Past
(86840, 135389, 237594, 'enUS', 'Highlord $p! Nearly all of our paladins have been called to fight the Void. I can only speculate why I was not among them.\n\nBut as a result, Scourge forces have built up quite a strong force around the chapel. Were it not for Darion\'s aid from Archerus, we would already be overrun, but holding the line is all they can do.\n\nGive us some room to breathe, Highlord--defeat as many of them as you can.', 0, 66102), -- Flickering Hope
(86733, 23504, 236779, 'enUS', 'So many have come to the defense of Silvermoon and the Sunwell. Names and faces I did not entirely expect... and some familiar faces I am glad to see.\n\nYou have my thanks for your part, $p.\n\nWe have Xal\'atath\'s forces held for now, but this is far from over.\n\nI would include you in our next steps. Meet me at the Sanctum of Light.', 0, 66102), -- Silvermoon Negotiations
(86558, 54203, 0, 'enUS', 'The Void here. It is like nothing else. I know you feel it, too. I\'m proud that you pulled through.\n\nWe must do something to stabilize the area. I\'m barely able to keep our escape route from imploding, and the rest of our scouts... I can only hope they can hold it together.\n\nOur ren\'dorei know what to do. They will place Shadestar Loci to protect this area, but will need your help activating them.', 0, 66102), -- Save a Piece of Mind
(86543, 54203, 0, 'enUS', 'We know there\'s land inside the Voidstorm, through its massive portal. If we can reach it, we can take the fight to Xal\'atath.\n\nI have found the key. It is a relic known as the Cynosure of Twilight. For ages, it has mystified us by revealing unreachable pathways to infinite unknowns. \n\nMy research tells me I can use it to open a path to the storm. \n\nThere\'s just one problem: it\'s in Magister\'s Terrace. And as you know, $p, we ren\'dorei are not exactly... in their good graces, at the moment.', 0, 66102); -- Magisters' Terrace: Homecoming

